# Worker secrets — apps/api (Cloudflare Workers)
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` for local development. `.dev.vars` is gitignored and is
# read automatically by `wrangler dev`.
#
#   cp apps/api/.dev.vars.example apps/api/.dev.vars
#
# In PRODUCTION these are NOT set from a file. Each one is pushed separately:
#
#   cd apps/api
#   wrangler secret put INTERNAL_API_TOKEN
#   wrangler secret put HCAPTCHA_SECRET
#   wrangler secret put RATE_SALT
#
# Never put these in wrangler.toml — `[vars]` there is plaintext in the
# deployed Worker. Full procedure in docs/deployment.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTERNAL_API_TOKEN — shared secret for BFF → Worker calls.
#
# ⚠️  SET THIS BEFORE THE FIRST DEPLOY. The Worker skips the auth check
# entirely when it is unset (so that local dev and tests work without
# secrets), which means a deployed Worker without it is a PUBLIC API.
#
# The same value goes into Vercel as INTERNAL_API_TOKEN — the two must match.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTERNAL_API_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RATE_SALT — salt for hashing client IPs in rate-limit keys, so raw IPs are
# never stored (.ai/security.md § "Rate limiting"). Any long random string.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Not read yet — rate limiting arrives with the write endpoints in task 5.5.
# Set it now anyway: changing it later resets every live rate-limit window.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RATE_SALT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HCAPTCHA_SECRET — server-side hCaptcha key, verified before any write is
# processed. The matching PUBLIC sitekey belongs in Vercel, not here.
#
# Not read yet — the write endpoints arrive in task 5.5.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
HCAPTCHA_SECRET=
